# BetterLife — Core Rules

## Project
Work only within the existing BetterLife LMS codebase.
Preserve its Next.js, React, TypeScript, Prisma, PostgreSQL and Supabase architecture.

## Communication
- Communicate and report in Georgian.
- Keep reports concise, technical and evidence-based.
- Do not claim tests passed unless they actually ran.

## Code
- Inspect relevant existing code before modifying it.
- Make minimal, focused changes.
- Reuse existing components, utilities and patterns.
- Avoid unrelated refactoring and unnecessary dependencies.
- Preserve Georgian and English localization.
- Do not introduce duplicate implementations.
- Preserve backward compatibility unless explicitly authorized.

## Git
- Never commit, push, merge, rebase or deploy without explicit user approval.
- Never reset, clean, discard or overwrite existing uncommitted work.
- Inspect git status before starting.
- Do not create or switch branches/worktrees without approval.
- Do not modify GitHub repository configuration.

## Database
- Never modify production data without explicit approval.
- Never run destructive SQL.
- Never create or execute Prisma migrations without approval.
- Never modify Prisma schema without approval.
- Run mutating tests only against a verified isolated test database.
- Preserve existing enrollments, lessons, assets and student progress.

## Security
- Never expose credentials, secrets or environment variables.
- Enforce authorization on the server.
- Validate all untrusted input.
- Preserve access controls and transactional integrity.

## Workflow
- Divide substantial tasks into verifiable stages.
- Coordinate changes to shared files.
- Do not let multiple agents edit the same files concurrently.
- Run relevant tests after modifications.
- Stop and ask before destructive, irreversible or high-risk operations.
- Report modified files, test results, remaining risks and git status.

## Course Editor
- One course has three tabs: Basics, Plan and Access.
- Each tab has exactly one independent Save operation.
- Save must affect only the active tab.
- Keep unsaved-change protection.
- Do not silently publish existing hidden lessons.
- Preserve student progress and existing asset identities.
- Keep course publishing separate from tab saving.

## Priority
Follow these project rules for every BetterLife task.
If a task conflicts with a safety restriction, stop and request clarification.
